 in a swim-up room* for a pool outside your door, or opt for a room with a whirlpool bath on your balcony*.\nHotel facilities\nHighlights\n7 x Bars\n1 x Kids pools\n3 x Pools\n7 x Restaurants\nAqua park\nThe Dine Around buffet restaurant\nSpa*\nPool\nThere are two pools, and one even has its own poolside bar. The main pool is lined with plenty of sun loungers and thatched umbrellas, with a mini island in the center. Plus, if you pick the right spot, you can soak up some sea views too.\nAqua park\nA wave pool, lazy river and a selection of slides are all at this aqua park, plus there's a splash zone for kids.\nKids' pool\nIndoor pool*\nThis pool is over at the spa and comes heated in winter.\nPool towels\nx3 outdoor pools\nThere are a trio of pools.\nKids' splash pool\nItems marked with * incur extra charges which are payable locally\n1\n/\n6\nFood & drink\nFoodies are well catered for, with a total of seven different restaurants. You've got the likes of a Greek taverna and an Indian place, and you can grill your own meal at The Stonegrill Steakhouse*. If you’re a fan of Asian food, there’s a restaurant* that serves Japanese, Thai and Chinese cuisine.\nThe Dine Around buffet restaurant\nThe main restaurant puts on buffet spreads for breakfast, lunch and dinner. There are live cooking stations and a kids' section, too.\nStone Grill restaurant*\nOpen for dinner, reservations required. Please note, this restaurant is not included as part of your All Inclusive package.\nKids' menu\nGreek Taverna\nBamboo Asian restaurant\nOpen for dinner only – meals are inspired from Asia and the Far East. You'll need to book a table in advance. Guests are entitled to 1 visit per stay, as part of their All Inclusive package.\nRestaurant dress code\nAppropriate attire in the restaurants. Swimwear and sportswear are not permitted in the evenings or lobby area.\nThe Terrace Bar\nBeach Bar\nSports Bar\nPool bar\n24-hour lobby bar\nView Bar\nOpening Times:\n[\n18.00-00.00\n]\nThis bar's just for grown ups. You can choose from a good selection of drinks including beer, wines and spirits as well as hot and cold soft drinks.\nChristmas gala meals\nA festive gala dinner buffet takes place in the Dine Around buffet restaurant. And there's an upgraded set menu in the à la carte restaurants. To help you celebrate in style, you’ll enjoy a variety of entertainment throughout the hotel, as well as being surrounded by New Year decorations and a truly festive atmosphere. It’s worth mentioning that pre-booking of the restaurants is required.\nSnack bar\nSari Restaurant\nThe Indian dishes are famous for herbs, spices, fresh fruit and vegetables and it's fair to say you'll get a good feel for this here. Guests are entitled to 1 visit per stay, as part of their All Inclusive package. A table reservation is required.\nA la carte dining\nReservations are required, minimum 48 hours in advance, via the kiosk screen in the lobby area.\nItems marked with * incur extra charges which are payable locally\n1\n/\n9\nEntertainment\nOnce the sun’s set, pull up a chair to watch a show or work your way around the seven watering holes. The Terrace Bar has an al fresco area that looks out over the sea, and there's a cocktail bar that's just for adults. The sports bar plays host to big screen TVs for watching the latest football games, as well as billiards tables*.\nEvening entertainment programme\nKids' club\nLive music\nLive sport screenings\nItems marked with * incur extra charges which are payable locally\n1\n/\n1\nSports & activities\nPack your active wear – this place has a football court and a tennis court. Down at the beach, you can join in with a game of volleyball, book on to some watersports* or go diving*.\nTennis court\nBeach volleyball\nMulti-sports court\nFootball\nAerobics\nScuba centre*\nBilliards*\nWatersports centre*\nPlayground\nItems marked with * incur extra charges which are payable locally\nHealth & beauty\nFacials, massages and body wraps are on offer at the spa*. And you can wind down before or after your treatment with a session in the sauna* or the steam room*.\nSpa*\nThe spa comes complete with a sauna, steam room, indoor pool and whirlpool bath.\nGym\nBeauty salon/treatments*\nHairdressing salon*\nItems marked with * incur extra charges which are payable locally\n1\n/\n4\nGeneral facilities\nLaundry service*\nFree limited Wi-Fi\nUp to 2 devices, per room, may access the free limited Wi-Fi quota. If you need a reliable Wi-Fi connection, the hotel offers this at an additional cost.\n24-hour room service*\nSafety deposit boxes\nSafe box is available, in the room, free of charge.\nReception area\nItems marked with * incur extra charges which are payable locally\nAccessibility\nThis hotel’s been surveyed by AccessAble so you can check if it’s suitable for your access needs.\nA Detailed Access Guide has been created with more information.\nWe realise everyone’s needs are different, so it’s best to get in touch with our Assisted Travel team if you’ve got any questions, on 0800 145 6920. The team are available from 9am to 7pm on weekdays, 9am to 5pm on Saturday and 10am to 5pm on Sunday.\nYou can also take a look at our other hotel Detailed Access Guides\n.\nAlso, if you or someone you’re travelling with requires assistance at the airport, or on your flight, please let us know as soon as possible once you’ve booked your holiday. You can give the Assisted Travel team a call to arrange this.\nLooking for more info?\nHead to our Accessible Holidays page\n.\nCalls from UK landlines cost the standard rate but calls from mobiles may be higher. Please check with your network provider.\nYour service at this hotel\nA TUI rep will make visits to your hotel. Holidays here also come with 24/7 support on the TUI app and by phone.\nFind out more about our service while you're away\nReasons to book with TUI\n24/7 support\nwhile you’re away\nprotected by\nATOL\nFinancially\nNo hidden\nfees\nFree kids’\nplaces\nHoliday dates & flights\nPrevio